# Security review — branch all-2026-11-25-1049 (86d22e2a..190fe55c, docs/plans/ excluded)

No high-confidence vulnerabilities found.

## Filtered (below the confidence threshold of 8, or excluded)

- `plugins/vwf/skills/plan/references/delta-checks.md:65` — command injection via
  `bootstrap config get repo.projects.<name>.folder --json` reads that put a registry
  project name into the key with no name check (also `doctor/references/stack-checks.md:67`,
  `init/references/new-repo.md:187`, `change-plan/references/recall-survey.md:57`).
  Dropped by the false-positive filter (confidence 8 that it is a false positive):
  every cited line exists at the base (bfbd53f2), the diff adds no `config get` line;
  hard exclusions 16 (markdown) and 7 (lack of a hardening measure); registry slugs
  are kebab-case and confirmed by the user (`architecture/references/stack-menu.md:101`).
  Possible follow-up: apply the key-name check to reads too.

The candidate pass also found: the `'\''` escape is correct for sh, bash, zsh and fish
once backslash and control characters are refused; `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$` admits no shell
metacharacter; `stack.mjs` prints no runnable command for a name that fails the check;
every changed `config set`, `--answer` and `add/remove tool` site quotes its values and
cites the rule.
